<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44764" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏpōrus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id. (<b>poet.</b>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging
				to sleep</i>, i. e., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Sleep-bringing</i>, <i>causing
			sleep</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 390</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2, 236</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 1,
				403</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">soporae pennae (Somni),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					10, 354</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnis, i. e. Lethe,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					13, 856</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Heavy with sleep</i>, <i>drowsy</i>,
				<i>dozy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dapibus vinoque soporus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 2, 222</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>